  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nActive weather pattern continues as an embedded MCV in the \nwesterlies tracks across Ohio. This MCV combined with moderate \ninstability was leading to strong storms across central Ohio. With \nhigh PWAT values there may still be some locally heavy rain, but the \nflooding threat looks to be more isolated. Some of the more robust \nstorms could produce strong to damaging winds across portions of \ncentral Ohio prior to pushing east of ILN/s area in the next hour or \nso. \n \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\nLow amplitude short wave will push a cold front into the area late\ntonight. Due to the orientation of the front from north-northeast to\nsouth-southwest it will be slow to move through the region. The\npotential for showers and storms will persist until this front \nclears. Some CAM solutions show better focus for storms across \nthe southern counties late tonight into Monday morning. \n\nPattern changes as broad long wave trough will move into the Great \nLakes toward mid week. This will push another cold front through the\nregion Wednesday night. Expect a change in air mass with highs \nin the 70s and lows in the 50s to lower 60s for Thursday and Friday.",
